2. Multi-line comments using '''
Python treats triple single quotes as a multi-line string, not a dedicated comment syntax. They are often used for documentation.

Example 1: Standalone multi-line string
'''This program demonstrateshow to print numbersusing a while loop.'''i = 1while i <= 5:    print(i)    i += 1



Example 2: Multiple lines of explanation
'''Employee Information ProgramThis program stores employee details.It displays employee name, age and salary.'''name = "John"age = 25salary = 30000print(name, age, salary)



3. Multi-line strings using """
Triple double quotes work in the same way as triple single quotes.

Example 1: Standalone multi-line string
"""This program calculatesthe sum of two numbers.It accepts two values and displays their sum."""a = 10b = 20print(a + b)



Example 2: Using triple double quotes as a docstring
